  "materialFindings": [
    "Viewed both actual decoded full RGB textures at their native tier sizes. They read as dark Gothic structural framing around painted/stained glass, with a coherent woodland/sky/water/bridge scene and distinguishable glass/frame finish. Fine colour detail remains readable; no added procedural grain, native-pixel contour grid or abstract material is relied upon.",
    "The owner-requested artist scene is interpreted within the glazing. The upper lobes, central quatrefoil, pointed framework, main mullion, lateral jambs and horizontal-bar rhythm remain representative of Low. Mid and High have the same forms from their shared source.",
    "Viewed both exact BOX comparisons at32x128 and16x64, including enlarged public comparison panels. Both tiers retain the dark pointed framework and pale-upper/darker-lower palette and feature scale. Scene detail differs, as authorized; resemblance rather than pixel equality is the criterion."
  ],
  "lowestPaneInterpretation": {
    "actualNativeObservation": "Two round/radial dark-gold motifs are discernible inside the lowest native panes. They are not claimed absent from Low. The new artist scene does not preserve those exact optical motifs.",
    "structuralAssessment": "Native pixels do not establish whether these small marks are painted/optical medallions or fine leaded ornament. They sit within the rectangular glazing rather than providing an unambiguous continuous heavy frame connection like the main mullion, came, arch or sill. It would overstate the evidence to call them proven projecting solid hardware.",
    "acceptanceReason": "Under the explicit owner request for an artist-depicted stained-glass scene, replacing this uncertain within-glass pattern is an allowed artwork interpretation. The actual rectangular pane boundaries and coarse dark olive/brown and warm optical masses remain representative in both BOX views. No new solid bottom rosettes are added. This acknowledges motif reinterpretation and uncertainty, rather than erasing a native feature by label.",
    "sourceContext": {
      "file": "docs/hexen2/textures/parallel-2026-10-20/stream-18-rtex018/independent-baseline-final-v1/verified-v1/lowest-pane-optical-context-and-BOX.png",
      "sha256": "33f00d619a2fe297af50501a73d8094448d85a5accfc0e60a9aead7441e94de3"
    },
